@startuml 04-item-states
!include style.iuml
title Work item life cycle (who or what moves it)

[*] --> proposed : PM: propose\nor coordinator: breakdown

proposed --> accepted : coordinator: accept
proposed --> deferred : coordinator: defer (reason)
proposed --> rejected : coordinator: reject (reason)
deferred --> accepted : coordinator: accept

accepted --> ready : coordinator: breakdown done\nor PM: prioritize\n(scope and outcome complete)
ready --> assigned : coordinator: assign\n[checks pass: collision, hold,\none open PR per engineer, upkeep share]
assigned --> in_progress : engineer: claim\n(branch, worktree, files)
in_progress --> in_progress : engineer: progress / note\nGitHub sync: new commit
in_progress --> in_review : engineer: ready\n[PR is ready on GitHub\nand contains main; no hold covers it]
in_review --> in_progress : coordinator: verdict changes\n(GitHub sync: PR back to draft)
in_review --> merged : GitHub sync: mergedAt seen\nor coordinator: merged (sha)
merged --> measured : engineer or PM: result\n(before, after, record, verdict)
measured --> validated : PM: validate\n(independent reference, record)
merged --> validated : PM: validate\n[upkeep item: no measure]

state blocked {
  blocked : blockedOn, unblockOn
}
assigned --> blocked : engineer: blocked
in_progress --> blocked : engineer: blocked
in_review --> blocked : coordinator: hold covers the PR
blocked --> in_progress : unblock event seen\nor coordinator: lift

in_progress --> ready : engineer: handover\nor clock: agent gone\n(assignee cleared)
assigned --> ready : clock: no claim in 1 block\nor coordinator: reassign

proposed --> cancelled : coordinator: cancel (reason)
accepted --> cancelled
ready --> cancelled
assigned --> cancelled
in_progress --> cancelled
rejected --> [*]
cancelled --> [*]
validated --> [*]

note right of ready
  Stage "planned" = accepted
  Stage "specified" = claim or scope
  Stage "implemented" = merged (commit from sync)
  Stage "tested" = ready with checks recorded
  Stage "validated" = validate with reference
end note
note left of in_review
  A prediction cannot change after claim.
  A result needs a committed record.
  Both refusals are events too.
end note
@enduml
